WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.944 --> 00:00:06.318
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.552 --> 00:00:17.120
PATRICK LECUYER:
Hi, I'm Patrick,

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.327
and I help customers in Montreal
learn about Google Cloud.

00:00:20.327 --> 00:00:22.410
I'm really excited to see
the launch of our newest

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.030
region in Montreal.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.300
This makes us the
15th GCP region

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.590
and means better
performance, lower latency,

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.410
and more flexibility
for local customers.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.000
With the opening
of this new region,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.100
Google Cloud Platform
products are now offered

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.645
and hosted from Montreal.

00:00:36.645 --> 00:00:38.400
This new region has
everything that you

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.960
need to build and scale.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.740
Our services include
compute, big data, storage,

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:45.510
and networking.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.282
Let's check out the demo.

00:00:48.282 --> 00:00:52.340
So from the main Google
Cloud Platform dashboard,

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.710
we'll go down the product
list and choose Storage.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.320
From Storage, we have the
option of creating a new bucket.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.960
We will create a new bucket.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.034
We'll call that bucket
our first-canadian-bucket.

00:01:05.034 --> 00:01:06.825
We want that bucket to
be regional storage,

00:01:06.825 --> 00:01:10.870
because we want the data to stay
within the new Montreal region.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.690
We'll scroll down
our list of regions

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.490
and choose
northamerica-northeast1,

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.225
which is the name of the
new Montreal-based region.

00:01:17.225 --> 00:01:21.110
We'll click to create
that new bucket.

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:24.990
I now have a bucket hosted
within our Montreal region.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.000
I just need to choose my file.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.440
I'll upload it to the bucket.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:29.820
And here we are.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:34.200
We have one file stored in
our new Montreal-based region

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.380
northamerica-northeast1.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:37.860
It's as easy as that.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.600
We've opened this
region in Montreal

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.200
because of the rising
demand for cloud services.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.900
Customers, such as Ubisoft,
Geotab, and Imagia,

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.160
just to name a few, have
leapt onto the cloud.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.020
As part of the Hieroglyphics
Initiative research project,

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.860
video game maker Ubisoft is
using Google Cloud Storage

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:56.390
to sort pictures and data of
ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:59.230
They use Compute Engine and ML
Engine to process and classify

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:02.310
that data with the goal of
accelerating our understanding

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.910
of this ancient language.

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:06.510
The new Montreal region means
more speed and availability

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:07.800
for Canadian customers.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.840
Here at Google,
we're here to help

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.270
you scale your business
the Google Cloud way.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.420
Contact to us.

